Input: {"question": "Which award did Advances in Meteorology receive?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 82, "text": "**Breaking News: Advances in Meteorology Earns Prestigious DOAJ Seal of Approval**"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 84, "end": 261, "text": "In a significant recognition of its commitment to open access and high publishing standards, the esteemed journal Advances in Meteorology has been awarded the coveted DOAJ seal."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 262, "end": 488, "text": "This prestigious mark of certification is bestowed by the Directory of Open Access Journals (DOAJ) to journals that demonstrate a high level of openness, adhere to best practices, and maintain exceptional publishing standards."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 489, "end": 660, "text": "\"We are thrilled to receive the DOAJ seal, which is a testament to our dedication to making high-quality research in meteorology accessible to a global audience,\" said Dr."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 661, "end": 720, "text": "Maria Martinez, Editor-in-Chief of Advances in Meteorology."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 721, "end": 887, "text": "\"Our team has worked tirelessly to ensure that our journal meets the highest standards of publishing excellence, and this recognition is a validation of our efforts.\""}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 888, "end": 1054, "text": "The DOAJ seal is a highly respected certification in the academic publishing community, with only a select few journals meeting the rigorous criteria set by the DOAJ."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1055, "end": 1284, "text": "To qualify for the seal, journals must demonstrate a strong commitment to open access, transparency, and accountability, as well as adhere to best practices in publishing, including peer review, licensing, and metadata standards."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1285, "end": 1512, "text": "\"Advances in Meteorology has consistently demonstrated a strong commitment to open access and high publishing standards, making it an exemplary model for journals in the field,\" said Lars Bjørnshauge, Managing Director of DOAJ."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1513, "end": 1696, "text": "\"We are pleased to award the DOAJ seal to this outstanding journal, and we look forward to continuing to work with them to promote open access and excellence in scholarly publishing.\""}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1697, "end": 1859, "text": "Data from the DOAJ website reveals that Advances in Meteorology has consistently met the criteria for the seal, with a perfect score in all categories, including:"}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1861, "end": 1956, "text": "* Open access: The journal provides immediate and unrestricted access to all published content."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1957, "end": 2087, "text": "* Peer review: Advances in Meteorology employs a rigorous peer-review process to ensure the highest quality of published research."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2088, "end": 2240, "text": "* Licensing: The journal uses Creative Commons licenses to ensure that authors retain copyright and readers have the freedom to reuse and share content."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2241, "end": 2387, "text": "* Metadata standards: The journal adheres to international metadata standards, ensuring that published content is easily discoverable and citable."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2388, "end": 2610, "text": "With this prestigious recognition, Advances in Meteorology solidifies its position as a leading journal in the field of meteorology, committed to promoting open access, transparency, and excellence in scholarly publishing."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 6, "text": "As Dr."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 7, "end": 132, "text": "Sofia Rodriguez stepped onto the stage, the warm applause of the packed auditorium enveloped her like a gentle summer breeze."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 133, "end": 337, "text": "She adjusted her glasses, her eyes shining with a mix of humility and pride, as she accepted the prestigious Belisario Domínguez Medal of Honor on behalf of the entire team behind Advances in Meteorology."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 338, "end": 390, "text": "The journal, founded by Sofia's mentor, the late Dr."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 391, "end": 485, "text": "Juan Hernandez, had been a beacon of innovation in the field of meteorology for over a decade."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 486, "end": 664, "text": "Its pages had witnessed the birth of groundbreaking research, from the development of more accurate storm surge models to the discovery of novel atmospheric circulation patterns."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 665, "end": 842, "text": "The journal's commitment to excellence had earned it a reputation as the go-to platform for scientists seeking to push the boundaries of weather forecasting and climate science."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 843, "end": 1022, "text": "As Sofia gazed out at the sea of faces, she couldn't help but think of the countless late nights, early mornings, and endless cups of coffee that had fueled the journal's success."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1023, "end": 1298, "text": "There was Maria, the meticulous editor who had a keen eye for detail; Jake, the whiz kid programmer who had developed the journal's cutting-edge submission system; and, of course, the countless authors and reviewers who had contributed their expertise to the journal's pages."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1299, "end": 1506, "text": "The Belisario Domínguez Medal of Honor, named after the Mexican physician and politician who had championed education and scientific progress, was a testament to the journal's tireless pursuit of excellence."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1507, "end": 1662, "text": "As Sofia held the medal aloft, its golden surface glinting in the light, she felt a sense of gratitude toward the entire Advances in Meteorology community."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1663, "end": 1737, "text": "In the days that followed, the journal's office was abuzz with excitement."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1738, "end": 1886, "text": "The team celebrated with a cake adorned with a fondant replica of the medal, and Maria even composed a triumphant haiku to commemorate the occasion:"}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1888, "end": 1913, "text": "\"Science shines so bright"}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1914, "end": 1937, "text": "Advances in Meteorology"}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1938, "end": 1963, "text": "Honored, proud, and free\""}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1965, "end": 2132, "text": "As the journal continued to break new ground, its pages would remain a testament to the power of collaboration, innovation, and dedication to the pursuit of knowledge."}}, "candidates": [{"candidate_id": "C0", "answer": "Belisario Domínguez Medal of Honor", "card_ids": ["d2:c0"]}], "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "Advances in Meteorology", "scope": "award", "claim": "Advances in Meteorology received the Belisario Domínguez Medal of Honor.", "answer": "Belisario Domínguez Medal of Honor", "quote": "She adjusted her glasses, her eyes shining with a mix of humility and pride, as she accepted the prestigious Belisario Domínguez Medal of Honor on behalf of the entire team behind Advances in Meteorology.", "original_document_number": 2}], "initial_answers": ["Belisario Domínguez Medal of Honor"]}
